ide.", "CONTROL GLUCÉMICO:Control Glucémico is the process of managing blood glucose levels in individuals with diabetes, which is a crucial aspect of their treatment. This management involves dietary adjustments and the administration of insulin to effectively regulate blood glucose levels. Throughout the treatment, maintaining appropriate control glucémico is essential for the patient's health, ensuring that their blood glucose levels remain stable. In particular, it has been noted that the control glucémico was adequate during treatment with NET (Nutritional Enteral Therapy) and NPT (Nutritional Parenteral Therapy), highlighting the importance of continuous monitoring and management of glucose levels in diabetic patients.", "TRATAMIENTO MÉDICO INTENSIVO:El tratamiento médico intensivo se refiere a las intervenciones médicas que se aplican a la paciente para el control de la diabetes tipo 2, complementando la cirugía bariátrica.", "ESTUDIO STAMPEDE:El estudio STAMPEDE es una investigación que demuestra la efectividad de la cirugía bariátrica en el control glucémico en pacientes obesos con diabetes tipo 2.", "ASOCIACIÓN AMERICANA DE DIABETES:The Asociación Americana de Diabetes (ADA) provides recommendations for diabetes management, including the possibility of surgery for certain patients.", "SOCIEDAD ESPAÑOLA DE LA CIRUGÍA DE LA ENFERMEDAD MÓRBIDA:The Sociedad Española de la Cirugía de la Enfermedad Mórbida is a society that collaborates with SEEDO to establish guidelines for metabolic surgery.", "KUMPF:Kumpf is a researcher whose work reflects the outcomes of patients after metabolic surgery, particularly regarding dietary changes and complications.", "DOBRATZ:Dobratz is a researcher who evaluated predictive equations for measuring basal metabolic expenditure in obese women.", "CIRUGÍA METABÓLICA:Metabolic surgery is a medical procedure recommended for treating type 2 diabetes in patients with obesity.", "FUGA ANASTOMÓTICA:Fuga anastomótica is a common complication after metabolic surgery that may require nutritional support due to its impact on oral intake.", "NAÚSEAS Y VÓMITOS:Nauseas y vómitos are common post-operative complications that can limit a patient's ability to eat normally after metabolic surgery.", "MALABSORCIÓN SEVERA:Malabsorción severa is a serious condition that can occur post-surgery, affecting nutrient absorption and necessitating nutritional support.", "EQUACIONES PREDICTIVAS:Ecuaciones predictivas are formulas used to estimate metabolic expenditure in patients, especially when calorimetry is unavailable.)<|COMPLETE|>", "SOCIEDAD AMERICANA DE NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL Y ENTERAL:The \"SOCIEDAD AMERICANA DE NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL Y ENTERAL\" (ASPEN) is an organization dedicated to advancing the field of nutritional support. It provides clinical guidelines for artificial nutritional support specifically for patients undergoing hematopoietic cell transplantation. Additionally, ASPEN offers guidelines for nutritional support tailored to hospitalized adult obese patients, with a particular focus on those undergoing bariatric surgery. Through these initiatives, ASPEN aims to enhance the quality of care and outcomes for patients requiring specialized nutritional interventions.", "UNIDAD DE CUIDADOS INTENSIVOS:The Intensive Care Unit (UCI) is a specialized department in hospitals where patients receive close monitoring and care, particularly for nutritional adjustments."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}